---
// What a visitor with JavaScript disabled sees instead of the raw platform
// error, on every public form.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// THE CONSTRAINT THIS COMPONENT EXISTS BECAUSE OF, STATED IN FULL
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// The deployment's edge platform refuses every POST whose body is one of the
// three encodings an HTML <form> can produce — application/x-www-form-
// urlencoded, multipart/form-data, or text/plain. This was confirmed against
// production, exhaustively, before this component was written:
//
//   · Correct Origin and Sec-Fetch-Site headers        -> still refused
//   · The full Sec-Fetch-Mode/-Dest/-User set a real browser sends for a
//     genuine top-level form navigation                -> still refused
//   · A cookie obtained from a real prior page visit,
//     attached to the POST                             -> still refused
//
// `application/json` is the one body type that passes through. `src/scripts/
// form-upgrade.ts` makes every form send that instead, and it works — but it
// is JAVASCRIPT that rewrites the submission, and there is no HTML attribute,
// no `enctype`, no header a static form can set that produces a JSON body.
// This is a hard limit of the web platform, not a gap this repository can
// close from the browser side. Only the platform setting itself, changed by
// whoever administers the deployment, removes the block for a script-free
// visitor.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// WHY <noscript>, AND WHY THAT IS THE RIGHT MECHANISM HERE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Content inside <noscript> is parsed and shown ONLY when the browser has
// scripting disabled or unsupported — there is no JS-side condition to keep in
// sync, and no way for this notice to appear for a visitor the JSON upgrade
// already serves correctly. A visitor running JavaScript never sees this,
// today or after any future change to this file.
//
// It renders BEFORE any submission is attempted, not after a failure — because
// a no-JS visitor's submission cannot be distinguished from a JS visitor's
// server-side (both are the identical HTTP request, since JavaScript is what
// would have rewritten it). Telling them beforehand is the only point at which
// this system can tell them at all.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// IT DOES NOT SWITCH THE FORM TO method="get". A GET carrying a name, an email,
// a date of birth or a cover letter would put every one of those into the URL —
// server logs, browser history, and any Referer header the next page sends —
// and GET requests carry none of the SameSite POST protections this site's CSRF
// defence relies on: a single image tag on any other site, pointed at the
// right URL with the right query string, could trigger one. Trading a real
// vulnerability for a smaller inconvenience is not an improvement.
//
// IT DOES NOT PRETEND THE FORM WILL WORK IF THEY TRY. The honest message is
// "this needs JavaScript, here is another way," not silence followed by a raw
// platform error the visitor cannot act on.

export interface Props {
  /**
   * What the visitor was about to submit, in a few words — "the individual
   * training enquiry", "your registration", "a coach application". Used only
   * in the sentence telling them what to put in the subject line.
   */
  what: string;
}

const { what } = Astro.props;
---

<noscript>
  <div class="njs-notice" role="alert">
    <p class="njs-lede"><strong>This form needs JavaScript to submit.</strong></p>
    <p>
      A technical restriction on this website currently blocks the plain
      submission a browser sends with scripting turned off — this is not
      something wrong with what you typed.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you cannot turn JavaScript on, email
      <a href="mailto:admin@mmakf.in">admin@mmakf.in</a> with “{what}” in the
      subject line and everything you wanted to submit in the body. The
      federation office will enter it for you.
    </p>
  </div>
</noscript>

<style>
  .njs-notice {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5, 1.25rem);
    padding: var(--space-4, 1rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-warn-border, #c99);
    border-left-width: 4px;
    border-radius: var(--radius, 6px);
    background: var(--c-warn-bg, #fdf6e8);
    max-width: 65ch;
  }
  .njs-notice p { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; }
  .njs-notice p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .njs-lede { font-size: 1.02rem; }
</style>
